{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1516747-tips-for-a-1-1-session","id":1516747,"title":"Tips for a 1:1 session","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-30T02:34:08-07:00","id":1516747,"title":"Tips for a 1:1 session","content":"Hey guys,<br /> <br /> I convinced my wife to give a try to TTRPG. So I wanted some tips for a 1:1 session. I am thinking to pre generate some characters so she can pick and don't worry about character creation. But I'm kind out of ideas for a one shot for just one person and completely new to TTRPG in general. I am hoping she has a really good time, so can really appreciate the hobby. Besides, I don't think I am a really good storyteller in general. <br /> <br /> So all things, I was hoping you guys could share some pieces of advices, on how to make things easy to learn and engage her as a single player experience, since she won't have other players to interact. General Storytelling Advice, and anything you guys consider could be relevant will be very much appreciated.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bThank you all in advance <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26883-imortalkiller","name":"ImortalKiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T06:44:46-07:00","id":1516770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ImortalKiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1516747-tips-for-a-1-1-session#post1516747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys,<br /> <br /> I convinced my wife to give a try to TTRPG. So I wanted some tips for a 1:1 session. I am thinking to pre generate some characters so she can pick and don't worry about character creation. But I'm kind out of ideas for a one shot for just one person and completely new to TTRPG in general. I am hoping she has a really good time, so can really appreciate the hobby. Besides, I don't think I am a really good storyteller in general.<br /> <br /> So all things, I was hoping you guys could share some pieces of advices, on how to make things easy to learn and engage her as a single player experience, since she won't have other players to interact. General Storytelling Advice, and anything you guys consider could be relevant will be very much appreciated.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bThank you all in advance <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> \u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, first off maybe <a href=\"https://christophedia.com/Repository/nWOD-COD/1E:%20Vampire%20-%20the%20Requiem/Demo/Danse%20de%20la%20Morte.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> will be useful to you. There are other SAS (Stand Alone Scenarios) pdfs around that might be of interest for you to ST or mine ideas from.<br /> All or most of them can be found in the <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers Vault</a> or Drivethrurpg.<br /> <br /> Beside this, not much in the way of tips that won't apply to STing in general - in fact having just one player instead of 3-6 possibly means much less trouble with balancing attention and so on, i guess. No big suggestions at the moment beside taking your time reading the corebook, storytelling section especially to get a feel of how you want to run things. hope tihs helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T14:07:37-07:00","id":1516822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1516747-tips-for-a-1-1-session?p=1516770#post1516770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, first off maybe <a href=\"https://christophedia.com/Repository/nWOD-COD/1E:%20Vampire%20-%20the%20Requiem/Demo/Danse%20de%20la%20Morte.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> will be useful to you. There are other SAS (Stand Alone Scenarios) pdfs around that might be of interest for you to ST or mine ideas from.<br /> All or most of them can be found in the <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers Vault</a> or Drivethrurpg.<br /> <br /> Beside this, not much in the way of tips that won't apply to STing in general - in fact 